# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The frontend's production values.
#
# This file DOES go to git, unlike every other .env: everything prefixed
# VITE_ ends up inside the bundle the browser downloads, so by definition there
# cannot be a secret here. Versioning it means the production build comes out
# the same whoever compiles it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Empty: the API is on the SAME origin as the page, and the generated client's
# paths already carry their `/api/v2`. Same origin and not another domain, for
# two reasons:
#   · Same origin ⇒ there is no CORS to configure.
#   · The refresh httpOnly cookie travels as a FIRST-party cookie, which is
#     what SameSite=Strict requires. With a different API domain, the browser
#     would treat it as third-party and would not send it.
VITE_API_ORIGIN=""
